Hi David,

I think this one is for you.

>Could be that the Sys Temp and CPU Temp labels need to be swapped.
>Check the order and values in your BIOS (if it prints them.)

I am pretty sure the order is ok. The Sys temp comes first in the bios, next 
the CPU temp. See the 'screenshot' of the hwmon page of the bios (! hope it 
isn't a problem including an attachment).
I also blocked the airflow through the CPU cooler during workload (video 
encoding) and the CPU temperature went up, whilst the Sys temp remained quite 
stable. 
Finally I did some measurements with my fingertips and a temperature sensor. 
In the case the reported temperatures where different, the 945PL chip was 
clearly warmer than the CPU. The only strange thing (to me in any case!) is 
that the absolute values differed quite a lot:
		lm_sensors	temp sensor	bios	finger
CPU		24 C		30 C		37 C	warm
Sys?(945PL)	38 C		50 C		38 C	hot

I am pretty sure the bios is wrong here with one of the values (I am not sure 
how that can be though!). Assuming that the Sys temperature measures the 
945PL chip, it was clearly a lot hotter than the CPU.

